| `aggregate_metrics()` | Transform | counts errors, tracks sessions, averages latency |
| `load_metrics()` | Load (SQLite) | creates tables, parameterised inserts |
| `render_html_report()` | Load (HTML) | builds report strings, writes file |
| `run_pipeline()` | Orchestration | wires the four together |

**Regex parsing** — four compiled patterns at module level (`ERROR_RECORD_RE`, `USER_RECORD_RE`, `API_RECORD_RE`, `WARN_RECORD_RE`) replace the fragile `.split()` chains. Each pattern captures named groups for extractor access without index brittle.

**Type hints + docstrings** — every function is annotated; every public-facing function has a docstring with args/return described.

**Dataclasses** — `ErrorRecord`, `UserRecord`, `ApiCallRecord`, `ParseResult`, `AggregatedMetrics` make the data flow explicit and mypy-verifiable. WARN lines are folded into error reporting (same as the original's `d_list` behavior).
